<div class="terms-document">
<p class="terms-intro">These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern the purchase and use of services provided by Signing Day Advisors (“SDA,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). By proceeding to payment and purchasing an SDA service, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to these Terms.</p>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>1. Services</h2>
<p>Signing Day Advisors provides college athletic recruiting guidance, assessments, educational materials, strategic recommendations, and related advisory services for student-athletes and their families.</p>
<p>The exact scope of services provided will depend on the service or package purchased by the client.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>2. No Guarantee of Admission, Recruitment, or Scholarship</h2>
<p>SDA provides advisory and educational services only. SDA does not guarantee any particular recruiting, admissions, scholarship, athletic, or academic outcome.</p>
<p>In particular, SDA does not guarantee:</p>
<ul>
<li>Admission to any college or university.</li>
<li>Recruitment by any college coach or athletic program.</li>
<li>An athletic scholarship or financial award.</li>
<li>A roster position or team placement.</li>
<li>Coach interest, communication, or response.</li>
<li>Any particular admissions or recruiting decision.</li>
</ul>
<p>All admissions, athletic recruiting, scholarship, and roster decisions are made independently by colleges, universities, coaches, athletic departments, admissions offices, and other third parties.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>3. Client Information</h2>
<p>SDA's assessments and recommendations depend on information provided by the student-athlete and family.</p>
<p>The client agrees to provide information that is accurate and complete to the best of their knowledge, including academic information, athletic performance, recruiting communications, test scores, college preferences, and other information requested by SDA.</p>
<p>SDA is not responsible for recommendations or conclusions affected by inaccurate, incomplete, outdated, or misleading information supplied by the client.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>4. SDA Compass</h2>
<p>The SDA Compass is an advisory recruiting assessment based on information available at the time the assessment is prepared.</p>
<p>Compass scores, classifications, school-fit assessments, rankings, and similar outputs are estimates intended to support recruiting strategy. They are not guarantees or predictions of admission, recruitment, scholarship, or roster placement.</p>
<p>Recruiting standards, admissions expectations, coaching staffs, team needs, roster availability, and athlete performance may change over time.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>5. Fees</h2>
<p>The client agrees to pay the price displayed for each selected service before SDA is required to perform that service.</p>
<p>Current advertised prices include:</p>
<ul>
<li>SDA Compass — $250.</li>
<li>Base Package — $1,000.</li>
<li>Premium Package — $2,000.</li>
<li>Monthly Subscription — $250 per month.</li>
</ul>
<p>Payment is processed through Stripe or another payment processor selected by SDA. SDA does not directly store complete payment-card information.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>6. Monthly Subscription and Automatic Renewal</h2>
<p>If the client purchases the SDA Monthly Subscription, the client authorizes a recurring charge of $250 per month.</p>
<p>The subscription automatically renews each month until cancelled.</p>
<p>Clients may cancel future renewals in accordance with the cancellation method provided by SDA. Cancellation prevents future recurring charges after the effective cancellation date.</p>
<p>Unless otherwise required by law or expressly stated by SDA, cancellation does not automatically create a refund for a billing period that has already begun.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>7. Refunds and Cancellations</h2>
<p>Refund eligibility for one-time services depends on whether SDA has begun performing or delivered the purchased service and on the refund policy presented at the time of purchase.</p>
<p>SDA reserves the right to decline refunds for services that have already been substantially performed or delivered, subject to applicable law.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>8. Student-Athletes Under 18</h2>
<p>If the student-athlete is under 18 years of age, the parent or legal guardian purchasing or authorizing the service represents that they have authority to enter into this agreement on behalf of the family.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>9. Client Responsibilities</h2>
<p>The student-athlete and family remain responsible for their own recruiting and admissions process.</p>
<p>This includes completing applications, communicating with coaches and schools, meeting deadlines, verifying information provided by third parties, attending meetings, and making final educational and recruiting decisions.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>10. Third-Party Information</h2>
<p>SDA may rely on publicly available or third-party information regarding colleges, athletic programs, recruiting standards, academic information, admissions criteria, athletic performance, and related matters.</p>
<p>SDA cannot guarantee that third-party information will always be complete, current, or error-free.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>11. Intellectual Property</h2>
<p>SDA materials, including assessments, reports, scoring methods, graphics, written resources, templates, recommendations, and SDA Compass materials, remain the intellectual property of Signing Day Advisors unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
<p>Clients may use materials provided to them for their own personal recruiting process. They may not reproduce, publish, resell, distribute, or commercially exploit those materials without SDA's written permission.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>12. Communications</h2>
<p>By providing contact information, the client authorizes SDA to communicate with the student-athlete, parent, or guardian regarding requested or purchased services.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>13. Independent Advisory Service</h2>
<p>Signing Day Advisors is an independent recruiting advisory service.</p>
<p>SDA is not an admissions office, college or university, athletic department, scholarship provider, or representative of any university unless expressly stated otherwise.</p>
<p>SDA is not affiliated with or endorsed by the NCAA, the Ivy League, any athletic conference, or any college or university unless expressly stated otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>14. Limitation of Liability</h2>
<p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, SDA will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or similar losses arising from recruiting, admissions, scholarship, athletic, or educational decisions made by the client or third parties.</p>
<p>Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>15. Changes to Services</h2>
<p>SDA may make reasonable changes to its methods, tools, processes, resources, or service delivery as its services develop.</p>
<p>Any material change affecting a service already purchased will not substantially reduce the core service promised to that client without agreement.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>16. Governing Law</h2>
<p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Massachusetts, to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p>
</div>
<div class="terms-block">
<h2>17. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions concerning these Terms, payments, services, cancellations, or account matters may be directed to:</p>
<p><strong>Signing Day Advisors</strong><br>Email: info@signingdayadvisors.com</p>
</div>
<p class="legal-note">By selecting “I Agree — Proceed to Payment,” you acknowledge that you have had an opportunity to review these Terms and agree to be bound by them. If you do not agree, do not proceed with purchasing SDA services.</p>
